From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: give up a disc menu's still picture

A Blu-ray menu often stands on a still: a clip of a single picture held
for as long as the menu is up. Its picture never reached the screen.
The player asks the decoder to drain once the clip has no more data, but
the decoder gives a picture only once its input buffer has filled past a
level - which one picture never does - and while draining it asks the
driver for one only when the driver's queue count says it holds some,
and that count reads none while the driver already has the picture
ready to hand over. With the menu's picture never shown, a disc's Java
program that waits for it stood on a black screen for good, and the
decoder was reset every five seconds as if it had hung.

Draining, the decoder now asks the driver for a picture on every call,
however little the buffer filled, and a drain with nothing to give is
not counted as a decoder that hangs. With no picture it answers as
before, so a drain early in a start - before the buffer first filled -
still waits for data rather than ending the stream. Outside a drain the
level and the queue count decide as before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
index bbbf5b2..66a5580 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -3704,7 +3704,11 @@ CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CAMLCodec::GetPicture(VideoPicture *pVideoPicture)
           amlVideoFile->IOControl(AMLVIDEO_IOC_GET_VFQ, &queued_frames) == 0 ? queued_frames : 0;
   }
 
-  if (m_buffer_level_ready && (buffer_level > m_minimum_buffer_level || (queued_frames > 0)) && (ret = DequeueBuffer()) == 0)
+  // Draining, what is decoded is owed however little filled the buffer - a disc menu's still is a
+  // clip of one picture - and is asked for: the queue count misses a picture the driver holds ready.
+  if ((m_drain ||
+       (m_buffer_level_ready && (buffer_level > m_minimum_buffer_level || queued_frames > 0))) &&
+      (ret = DequeueBuffer()) == 0)
   {
     pVideoPicture->iFlags = 0;
 
@@ -3749,7 +3753,8 @@ CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CAMLCodec::GetPicture(VideoPicture *pVideoPicture)
   }
   else if ((m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready) || (buffer_level > (streambuffer ? 100.0f : 10.0f)))
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_NONE;
-  else if (ret != EAGAIN || elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(m_decoder_timeout))
+  else if (ret != EAGAIN ||
+           (!m_drain && elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(m_decoder_timeout)))
   {
     CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "CAMLCodec::GetPicture: time elapsed since last frame: {:d}ms ({:d}:{})",
       elapsed_since_last_frame.count(), ret, strerror(ret));
